course: dictionary
lesson: 4888
title: Igloo and its two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Igloo» has a main meaning: a dome-shaped shelter built from blocks of hard snow. Context clues, the words around the word, show you which meaning is being used.
explain: Read this: «The Inuit of the Arctic... in winter some built snow houses called igloos.» The clues are snow houses and Arctic, so an igloo is a snow shelter where people lived in the far north. The sentence also says most Inuit did not live in igloos all year, so they were not the only homes.
explain: The word can also mean anything shaped like a dome, such as a dome-shaped tent or bin. A clue like «shaped like a dome» tells you that this second meaning is in use, and not the snow shelter.
fact: «Igloo» means a dome-shaped shelter built from blocks of hard snow.
fact: The Inuit people of the Arctic built igloos, especially for hunting trips.
fact: Snow is a good insulator: it keeps heat in, so an igloo can be much warmer inside than outside.
fact: «Igloo» can also mean anything shaped like a dome.
fact: Most Inuit did not live in igloos all year; they also lived in houses of stone, turf and skins.
exercise: «In winter some built snow houses called igloos.» What is an igloo? | A stone house with a flat roof | A sled pulled by dogs | A boat used for hunting seals | *A dome-shaped shelter built from blocks of hard snow
exercise: «The Inuit of the Arctic hunted seals and whales, and built snow houses called igloos.» Find and copy one word that tells you where the Inuit lived. | whales | *Arctic | sleds | kayaks
exercise: Ella says her new tent is an igloo because it is shaped like a dome. What does igloo mean here? | A boat for hunting | *Anything shaped like a dome | A cold, icy wind | Blocks of hard snow for building
test: Why is an igloo warmer inside than the cold air outside? | Snow melts into water at once | Snow lets heat out quickly | *Snow is a good insulator and keeps heat in | Snow gives out light, so it glows
test: «Most did not live in igloos all year.» What does this tell you about igloos? | They were built only for children to play in | They were always made of stone and turf | *They were used in some seasons and were not the only homes | They were the only homes the Inuit ever had
exam: Jayden guesses a new word and wants to check it. Which is the best way to check a meaning? | Guess a different word every time | *Swap the meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Say the word loudly three times | Skip the sentence and never read it again
